From: SKJ Wine <skj-tech@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] secur32: Look for machine keyset containers in HKLM.

get_key_blob() only opened the rsaenh key container under HKEY_CURRENT_USER.
rsaenh stores CRYPT_MACHINE_KEYSET containers under HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, so a
TLS server using a certificate from LocalMachine\My (the normal place for a
service's certificate) failed AcquireCredentialsHandle and dropped every
connection. Seen with SteelSeries GG (GGEZ server on 127.0.0.1:6327).
---
diff --git a/dlls/secur32/schannel.c b/dlls/secur32/schannel.c
index 1e149d7..3bdea29 100644
--- a/dlls/secur32/schannel.c
+++ b/dlls/secur32/schannel.c
@@ -603,6 +603,8 @@ static BYTE *get_key_blob(const CERT_CONTEXT *ctx, DWORD *size)
 
     if (!(path = get_key_container_path(ctx))) return NULL;
     retval = RegOpenKeyExW(HKEY_CURRENT_USER, path, 0, KEY_READ, &hkey);
+    /* rsaenh keeps CRYPT_MACHINE_KEYSET containers under HKLM */
+    if (retval) retval = RegOpenKeyExW(HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, path, 0, KEY_READ, &hkey);
     free(path);
     if (retval)
         return NULL;
